      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white border-b border-slate-800 pb-2">
        Loss-Versus-Rebalancing (LVR) Theory: The Fundamental Mathematics of AMM Toxicity
      </h2>
      <p>
        The traditional metric of <em>Impermanent Loss (IL)</em> measures an LP's portfolio value relative to a static buy-and-hold benchmark. However, seminal quantitative research by Milionis, Moallemi, Roughgarden, and Timmer (2022) revealed that IL is path-independent and fundamentally flawed for dynamic strategy evaluation.
      </p>
      <p>
        The true economic cost incurred by concentrated liquidity providers is <strong>Loss-Versus-Rebalancing (LVR)</strong>. LVR quantifies the cumulative rents extracted by informed high-frequency arbitrageurs who continuously pick off stale AMM quotes whenever prices move on centralized exchanges (Binance, Coinbase). Under continuous Black-Scholes geometric Brownian motion dynamics ($dS_t = \mu S_t dt + \sigma S_t dW_t$), the instantaneous LVR rate is derived as:
      </p>

      <pre is:raw class="bg-slate-950 p-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-800 text-xs font-mono text-amber-300 overflow-x-auto"><code>dLVR / dt = (sigma^2 / 8) * S * L
</code></pre>

      <p>
        Where:
      </p>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-slate-300 list-disc pl-5">
        <li><code>sigma</code> is the annualized instantaneous volatility of the underlying asset pair.</li>
        <li><code>S</code> is the instantaneous spot price of the asset.</li>
        <li><code>L</code> is the total active liquidity depth provided within the active tick range.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        For an LP position to generate positive economic expected value ($E[\Pi] &gt; 0$), the earned fee revenue rate must strictly exceed the instantaneous LVR drain:
      </p>

      <pre is:raw class="bg-slate-950 p-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-800 text-xs font-mono text-amber-300 overflow-x-auto"><code>Fee_Revenue_Rate = Fee_Tier * Swap_Volume_Rate > (sigma^2 / 8) * S * L
</code></pre>

