      </h2>
      <p>
        By restricting liquidity to a tight price band $[P_a, P_b]$ around current spot price $P$, an LP provides the same effective market depth as an infinitely funded v2 pool while depositing only a fraction of the capital.
      </p>
      <p>
        The formal capital efficiency multiplier ($M$) relative to Uniswap v2 is given by:
      </p>

      <pre is:raw class="bg-slate-950 p-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-800 text-xs font-mono text-amber-300 overflow-x-auto"><code>Capital Efficiency Multiplier (M) = 1 / (1 - (Pa / Pb)^(1/4))
</code></pre>

      <p>
        For example:
      </p>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-slate-300 list-disc pl-5">
        <li>For a stablecoin pair (USDC/USDT) bounded tightly between $[0.999, 1.001]$, the capital efficiency multiplier $M \approx 4,000\times$. A $25,000 position captures the fee yield of a $100,000,000 v2 position.</li>
        <li>For an ETH/USDC pool operating within a $\pm 10\%$ range ($[2,700, 3,300]$ at $3,000), $M \approx 20\times$.</li>
        <li>For a wide $\pm 50\%$ range ($[1,500, 4,500]$), $M \approx 4.2\times$.</li>
      </ul>

